*Infinite [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Heavenly Tower boss duo may seem unstoppable, but due to the constant stream of unbuffed [[Kang Roo]]s and the Mooth at the start, this stage provides enough money to make it manageable. Anti-traitless crowd-controllers like [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]] are pretty much mandatory to stall the enemies and beat this stage. If you've been progressing through [[Legend Stages|Uncanny Legends]], [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Dogumaru]] will be a great asset as well with its high health, resistance to traitless enemies, warp immunity, and good attack power, but be wary of his long attack animation.

[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] are good and quick damage dealers, while [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] can act as meatshields. Additionally, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] will help out a lot by blocking Hermit's waves. The Kang Roo spam allows you to bring Cat CPU without worries of bankruptcy, but you might want to turn it off when Macho Crystal recharges so it doesn't hit Kang Roo. Rich Cat is recommended if you still struggle with money, Worker Cat upgrades are expensive enough to drain your cash. Finally, Sniper the Cat and the Breakerblast [[Cat Cannon|Cannon]] can help push the enemies back.

Do not bring [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]] unless you have him at level 60 or above total, as he will be unable to survive a Yulala hit; even then, he remains inconsistent as Hermit will destroy him immediately after. Instead, it is recommended to use [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] with wave immune and preferably survive talents, as he's significantly more durable, cheaper, and only needs to be level 51+ to survive a Yulala hit.

This stage can be CPU'd, albeit inconsistently. Bring a load out containing [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], Rock Cat, Macho Crystal Cat, Fishman Cat, Supercat, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]], Bullet Train Cat, Tourist Cat, and [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]], as well as a Rich Cat and Slow Cannon. If you have him, [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]] can take the place of Hitman for much more consistent results.

